# Day 11 – Chain Rule

## 📌 Concept
Chain Rule is used when one quantity depends on another through an intermediate variable.

## 📐 Formula

dy/dx = (dy/du) × (du/dx)

## ✏️ Example

Given:

y = u²  
u = 2x + 3

Using Chain Rule:

dy/dx = 2u × 2

dy/dx = 4u

For x = 5:

u = 2(5) + 3  
u = 13

Therefore,

dy/dx = 4 × 13  
dy/dx = 52

## 💡 Key Point

Differentiate step-by-step and multiply the derivatives.

